WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:17.640
Bill Sikes dragged Oliver through the narrow streets so quickly that Nancy had trouble keeping up.

2
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.401
"Grab hold of her hand," Sikes said roughly to Oliver.

3
00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.842
"And don't you dare make a sound."

4
00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:27.703
They were in a dark corner, out of view of any passersby.

5
00:00:28.803 --> 00:00:31.024
Oliver realized there was no point in resisting.

6
00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:34.529
He held out his hand, which Nancy clasped tightly.

7
00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:37.790
"Give me the other hand," said Sikes.

8
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:39.770
"Here, Bull's-eye!"

9
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.811
he called to the white dog.

10
00:00:42.771 --> 00:00:44.111
The dog looked up and growled.

11
00:00:44.131 --> 00:00:45.992
"See here, dog.

12
00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:49.513
If this boy cries out, grab him and hold on tight.

13
00:00:50.473 --> 00:00:51.233
Do you understand?"

14
00:00:52.294 --> 00:00:54.694
The dog looked menacingly at Oliver and growled again.

15
00:00:55.775 --> 00:00:57.475
They set off again into the dark night.

16
00:00:58.455 --> 00:01:00.876
The lights in the shops were dim through the heavy mist.

17
00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:05.378
Bill was dragging Oliver past the prison when a church bell struck the hour.

18
00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.921
"I wonder whether the prisoners can hear that," said Nancy.

19
00:01:09.941 --> 00:01:13.103
"Of course they can," replied Sikes.

20
00:01:14.163 --> 00:01:17.845
"The last time I was locked up for housebreaking, I could hear every sound at night."

21
00:01:17.865 --> 00:01:22.028
"Poor fellows," said Nancy, who was still looking at the prison.

22
00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:24.950
But there wasn't time to think about prisoners.

23
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:28.872
Sikes yanked on Oliver's wrist, and Nancy came along too.

24
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.121
They walked through deserted streets for half an hour.

25
00:01:33.322 --> 00:01:37.383
At last they stopped in front of a run-down house with an ancient "For Rent" sign on the

26
00:01:37.423 --> 00:01:39.765
door. Nancy rang the bell.

27
00:01:40.925 --> 00:01:45.327
Then they crossed the street and stood under a streetlamp so someone inside could see who they were.

28
00:01:46.488 --> 00:01:48.268
At last the door softly opened.

29
00:01:49.449 --> 00:01:53.531
Sikes seized a terrified Oliver by the collar, and they went quickly inside the house.

30
00:01:54.651 --> 00:01:55.892
The hallway was very dark.

31
00:01:57.644 --> 00:02:00.206
They waited while the person who had let them in barred the door.

32
00:02:01.166 --> 00:02:02.367
Then he lit a candle.

33
00:02:03.428 --> 00:02:04.529
It was the Artful Dodger.

34
00:02:05.589 --> 00:02:07.591
He grinned at Oliver but didn't say anything.

35
00:02:08.672 --> 00:02:10.953
He led them downstairs and through an empty kitchen.

36
00:02:11.954 --> 00:02:16.097
When he opened the door to a low room, they were greeted with shouts of laughter from Charley

37
00:02:16.117 --> 00:02:18.778
Bates. "Oh, my goodness!"

38
00:02:19.159 --> 00:02:19.799
cried Charley.

39
00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:21.600
"Here he is!

40
00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:23.602
Look at him, Fagin!

41
00:02:24.542 --> 00:02:26.684
Hold me, somebody, or I'll die laughing."

42
00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:31.173
At this, Charley fell on the floor and rolled around and laughed some more.

43
00:02:32.253 --> 00:02:36.414
Then he jumped up and held the candle so close to Oliver's new jacket that it nearly caught

44
00:02:36.494 --> 00:02:39.235
fire. "Look at his clothes, Fagin!

45
00:02:40.275 --> 00:02:42.276
Superfine cloth and a stylish cut!

46
00:02:43.316 --> 00:02:44.356
And his books too.

47
00:02:45.397 --> 00:02:46.877
He's such a gentleman now."

48
00:02:46.897 --> 00:02:52.639
"Delighted to see you looking so well," Fagin said to Oliver with mock humility.

49
00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:57.440
"Why didn't you write, my dear, and say you were coming?

50
00:02:58.528 --> 00:03:00.149
We'd have warmed something up for supper."

51
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.951
Oliver was too shaken to respond.

52
00:03:03.952 --> 00:03:06.814
He didn't even react when the Dodger started going through his pockets.

53
00:03:07.955 --> 00:03:08.576
"What's this?"

54
00:03:08.976 --> 00:03:11.398
cried the Dodger, holding up the five-pound note that Mr.

55
00:03:11.418 --> 00:03:12.478
Brownlow had given Oliver.

56
00:03:12.498 --> 00:03:16.762
"That's mine, Fagin," said Sikes as Fagin seized the note.

57
00:03:17.962 --> 00:03:19.884
"No, it's mine," said Fagin.

58
00:03:19.904 --> 00:03:22.286
"You shall have the books, Bill."

59
00:03:22.306 --> 00:03:26.116
"Hand it over," said Sikes.

60
00:03:26.136 --> 00:03:29.878
"Do you think Nancy and I have nothing to do but kidnap every boy that escapes from you?

61
00:03:30.978 --> 00:03:33.499
If you don't give me that money, I'll take the boy back again."

62
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.020
Fagin started in surprise.

63
00:03:37.121 --> 00:03:39.062
Oliver started too, but for a different reason.

64
00:03:40.762 --> 00:03:44.384
He hoped that their dispute might really result in his being taken back to Mr.

65
00:03:44.404 --> 00:03:47.765
Brownlow. Sikes plucked the note from Fagin's hand.

66
00:03:48.846 --> 00:03:53.108
Looking the old man coolly in the face, Sikes folded up the note and tied it in his

67
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.042
neckerchief. "That's for our share of the trouble," he said.

68
00:03:57.062 --> 00:04:00.604
"Keep the books and sell them if you're not fond of reading."

69
00:04:00.624 --> 00:04:04.467
"They're very pretty," said Charley, pretending to read one.

70
00:04:04.487 --> 00:04:07.249
"Beautiful writing, isn't it, Oliver?"

71
00:04:07.269 --> 00:04:11.853
"They belong to the kind gentleman who took care of me," said Oliver in distress.

72
00:04:11.873 --> 00:04:15.796
"I would have died from the fever if it weren't for him and the housekeeper.

73
00:04:16.857 --> 00:04:18.578
Oh, please send back the books and the money.

74
00:04:19.639 --> 00:04:21.200
The gentleman will think I stole them."

75
00:04:22.292 --> 00:04:25.614
With these pleading words, Oliver fell on his knees in front of Fagin.

76
00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:28.435
"You're right, Oliver."

77
00:04:29.456 --> 00:04:31.197
Fagin looked around at the others in the room.

78
00:04:31.217 --> 00:04:34.499
"This couldn't have happened better if we'd planned it."

79
00:04:34.519 --> 00:04:37.981
"But they won't go looking for him," said Sikes.

80
00:04:39.041 --> 00:04:40.262
"They're soft-hearted people.

81
00:04:41.162 --> 00:04:44.624
They know if he's found, they'll have to bring charges and he'll get sent to prison."

82
00:04:45.765 --> 00:04:47.506
Oliver looked from one person to the other.

83
00:04:48.686 --> 00:04:53.373
Suddenly he jumped to his feet and tore wildly from the room, uttering shrieks for help that made

84
00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:54.494
the old house echo.

85
00:04:54.514 --> 00:04:57.255
"Don't let the dog go after him, Bill."

86
00:04:58.356 --> 00:05:02.678
Nancy sprang to the door and closed it as Fagin, the Dodger, and Charley ran after Oliver.

87
00:05:02.698 --> 00:05:05.240
"The dog will tear him to pieces."

88
00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.721
"That would serve him right."

89
00:05:08.822 --> 00:05:11.183
Sikes grabbed Nancy's wrists and they began to struggle.

90
00:05:11.203 --> 00:05:13.384
"What's the matter here?"

91
00:05:13.705 --> 00:05:16.086
cried Fagin as he and the boys returned with Oliver.

92
00:05:16.106 --> 00:05:21.076
"The girl's gone mad," said Sikes.

93
00:05:21.096 --> 00:05:23.097
"No, she hasn't," retorted Nancy.

94
00:05:24.297 --> 00:05:26.018
Fagin turned his attention to Oliver.

95
00:05:26.038 --> 00:05:29.520
"So you wanted to get away from me, my dear?

96
00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.481
Wanted to call the police for assistance?"

97
00:05:33.661 --> 00:05:35.762
He picked up a club lying near the fireplace.

98
00:05:35.782 --> 00:05:38.183
"We'll cure you of that."

99
00:05:39.344 --> 00:05:41.845
Nancy rushed forward and flung the club into the fire.

100
00:05:42.965 --> 00:05:45.766
"I won't stand by and let you hurt him," she shouted.

101
00:05:46.727 --> 00:05:49.968
"He's a thief, a liar, and all that's bad from this night forward.

102
00:05:51.024 --> 00:05:51.825
Isn't that enough?"

103
00:05:52.905 --> 00:05:55.327
"You're a fine one to talk," said Sikes.

104
00:05:55.347 --> 00:05:57.328
"I know I am."

105
00:05:58.409 --> 00:05:59.870
Nancy turned her anger on Fagin.

106
00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:03.552
"I've thieved for you ever since I was half as old as Oliver.

107
00:06:04.633 --> 00:06:06.554
I know what kind of life you're leading him into.

108
00:06:07.655 --> 00:06:09.196
You're the wretch who ruined my life."

109
00:06:10.377 --> 00:06:11.938
And with that, she rushed at Fagin.

110
00:06:12.999 --> 00:06:16.901
She probably would have pummeled him with her fists if Sikes hadn't grabbed her and held her back.

111
00:06:18.682 --> 00:06:20.744
Nancy struggled for a moment and then fainted.

112
00:06:21.896 --> 00:06:24.078
Fagin wiped his forehead and smiled at Oliver.

113
00:06:24.098 --> 00:06:26.940
"Charley, show Oliver to bed."

114
00:06:27.941 --> 00:06:30.022
"He shouldn't wear his best clothes tomorrow, should he?"

115
00:06:30.402 --> 00:06:31.003
asked Charley.

116
00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:34.205
"Certainly not," Fagin replied.

117
00:06:35.306 --> 00:06:39.129
Charley led Oliver into the kitchen where there were several sacks on the floor for beds.

118
00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.552
And here Charley produced the old clothes that Oliver had given to Mr.

119
00:06:43.572 --> 00:06:44.372
Brownlow's servant.

120
00:06:44.392 --> 00:06:50.036
"Fagin knows everyone who's got clothes for sale," explained Charley.

121
00:06:50.056 --> 00:06:52.277
"He came upon yours and knew you'd want them back."

122
00:06:53.397 --> 00:06:55.998
Oliver took off his new clothes and handed them to Charley.

123
00:06:56.018 --> 00:06:58.259
"What fun this is!"

124
00:06:58.659 --> 00:06:59.299
said Charley.

125
00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:04.981
Then he departed from the room, leaving Oliver in the dark and locking the door behind him.
